{% extends 'site/base_public.html.twig' %}

{#
   The aggregated calendar.

   🔴 **It is READ-ONLY since S146c.** It used to be a resource grid with a checkbox
   list of every machine and space and a booking draft on top — a second way to book,
   competing with the resource's own page. Booking belongs to the thing being booked
   (`/machines/{id}`, `/places/{id}`, S146b); this page answers what is going on here
   and when it is open. `booking: false` in the payload is the whole mechanism.

   ⚠️ **It owns no calendar code of its own (S146a).** The grid, the week and month
   views and the opening-hours rules come from `site/_calendar.html.twig`, driven by
   the `calendar` Stimulus controller and the payload `App\Calendar\CalendarPayload`
   builds. This file decides the WORDS — the same split as the catalogues.

   🔴 **Why that mattered enough to do first.** This template and
   `machine-calendrier.html.twig` used to carry twelve identically-named JavaScript
   functions each. S134d and S134e had to edit the same opening-hours rule in both,
   four times, in one session — and the calendar disagreeing with the booking gate
   about when the lab is open is the exact fault the schedule model was rebuilt to
   prevent.

   ⚠️ **The location tiles are new here (S146a).** Every catalogue got a location
   filter in S137/S138; the calendar never had one, though "which location is this"
   is most of the reason locations exist. Choosing one re-renders the page, because
   the opening hours, the exceptions and the bookable resources all change with it.
#}

{% block title %}{{ 'nav.whats_on'|trans }} - FabOS{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/calendar-leaderboard.css') ~ '?v=20260709-calheader-userlogo' }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/calendar-fix.css') }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/calendar-modern.css') ~ '?v=20260820-s146a' }}">
    {# The location tiles are the catalogues' `ml-*` filter row, not a shape of
       their own — same markup, same sheet, so a change to the filter row reaches
       the calendar too. #}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/machines-list.css') ~ '?v=20260820-s146a' }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}

    <main class="main-content calendar-modern-page">
        <section class="container calendar-shell"
                 data-controller="calendar"
                 data-calendar-payload-value="{{ calendar|json_encode }}">
            <div class="calendar-hero">
                <div>
                    <span class="calendar-eyebrow">{{ 'cal.planning'|trans }}</span>
                    {# ⚠️ The location's NAME is the headline when one is chosen. The
                       page is about a place now, and "Ce qui se passe" above a grid of
                       one location's week says less than the location itself does. #}
                    <h1>{{ venueContext.selected ? venueContext.selected.name : 'cal.activity_title'|trans }}</h1>
                    <p>{{ 'cal.activity_subtitle'|trans }}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="calendar-actions">
                    {% if app.user %}
                        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ path('app_my_reservations') }}">{{ 'resv.title'|trans }}</a>
                    {% else %}
                        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ path('app_login') }}">{{ 'nav.login'|trans }}</a>
                    {% endif %}
                    {# ⚠️ These are where booking WENT. A read-only calendar that does
                       not say where to book is a dead end, and the sentence above alone
                       is not a control. #}
                    {% if feature_enabled('places') %}<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ path('app_places') }}">{{ 'nav.places'|trans }}</a>{% endif %}
                    {% if feature_enabled('machines') %}<a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ path('app_machines') }}">{{ 'resv.see_machines'|trans }}</a>{% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="calendar-stats" aria-label="{{ 'cal.summary'|trans }}">
                <article class="calendar-stat-card"><span>{{ 'cal.today_hours'|trans }}</span><strong data-calendar-target="todayHours">{{ 'cal.loading'|trans }}</strong></article>
                <article class="calendar-stat-card"><span>{{ 'cal.reservations_today'|trans }}</span><strong data-calendar-target="todayCount">0</strong></article>
                <article class="calendar-stat-card"><span>{{ 'cal.events_upcoming'|trans }}</span><strong>{{ upcomingEventCount }}</strong></article>
                <article class="calendar-stat-card"><span>{{ 'cal.next_slot'|trans }}</span><strong data-calendar-target="nextSlot">{{ 'cal.select'|trans }}</strong></article>
            </div>

            {# 🔴 **The machine grid is GONE (S146c).** This page carried a checkbox
               list of every machine and space, a search box and a status filter, so
               that a resource grid could be narrowed down to one thing — which is a
               worse version of that thing's own page, and the page it competed with
               now carries the same calendar (S146b). Deleting it is what makes this
               screen about the LOCATION rather than about equipment.

               ⚠️ The resources still reach the component: they are how a booking is
               matched to this location and named on its card. What went is the UI for
               filtering them. #}
            <div class="calendar-workspace is-single">
                {# ⚠️ The board's words are view-neutral AND read-only. They used to
                   say "Semaine de réservation" and, after S146a, "click an open slot
                   to book" — a sentence describing a control this page no longer has.
                   ⚠️ **"Au programme" is the operator decision the roadmap parked**:
                   name no type, because each card now names its own kind through its
                   category (S146f). That is what made it safe to choose. #}
                {% include 'site/_calendar.html.twig' with {
                    heading: 'cal.board_title'|trans,
                    subtitle: 'cal.board_desc'|trans,
                    venue_context: venueContext,
                    venue_route: 'app_calendar',
                    venue_query: app.request.query.all,
                } only %}
            </div>

            {# 🔴 **The booking draft is GONE (S146c).** `booking: false` in the
               payload is what makes the grid read-only — no click target, no `+`
               affordance — and the dialog is simply not rendered. Booking belongs to
               the thing being booked. #}
        </section>

    </main>
{% endblock %}

{% block javascripts %}
    <script src="{{ asset('js/main.js') ~ '?v=20260811-s134c-i18n' }}"></script>
{% endblock %}
